  "created_at": "2026-03-19T00:00:00.000Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-03-19T00:00:00.000Z",
  "_migration_notes": {
    "migrated_from": "pullback_uptrend_entry_composite_v2",
    "why_stateless_was_wrong": "The MACD divergence timing stage is event-based, but the stateless engine re-evaluates the same divergence on every bar prefix after the confirming swing pair exists. That causes duplicate entries for the same divergence event and misattributes timing in backtests. The regime gate itself is stateless-safe; the broken piece is the divergence timing.",
    "expected_effect_on_backtest": "Trade count should drop because repeated entries from the same divergence event disappear. Expectancy may improve or remain similar if the removed duplicates were mostly churn around the original signal.",
    "remaining_limitation": "This relies on MACD divergence continuing to fire across the short watch window. A future improvement would be an explicit divergence_confirmed event from the primitive so the watch phase can open on the confirmation bar and emit only on downstream trigger conditions."
  },
